    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0940" n="840" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg840"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/103: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sydney</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sydney</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-05-16T15:00:00+10:00">May 16, 1934—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 16—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram May 15, 6 p.m., sentence in Department’s telegram May 5, 2
                    p.m., was correctly received and repeated in my telegram of May 10, 5 p.m.</p>
                <pb facs="0941" n="841" xml:id="pg841"/>
                <p>The question is whether damage to American transportation interests is not caused
                    by Australian Customs Act of 1901<anchor n="14" xml:id="d675-f1"/> rather than
                    by Canadian agreement of 1931. It would seem that diversion of freight from
                    American to Canadian lines was due to provisions of Customs Act and occurred
                    prior to and irrespective of Canadian agreement; that Canadian agreement merely
                    made it no longer advantageous for Canada to divert some of her freight to
                    American lines, our loss on this account being relatively unimportant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
